{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "registry-signing-v1",
  "description": "Conformance vectors for the exchange registry signature. For each vector, take the five fields version, lastVerified, validUntil, source and entries of registry, build the document { format: 1, issuedAt, registry, sequence } from the envelope in signature, write it as canonical JSON (keys in UTF-16 code unit order, no whitespace, integers only), prefix it with the label and a newline, and check the Ed25519 signature (base64, exactly 64 bytes, canonical encoding) against each of publicKeys. A document is accepted only when a key verifies it, its sequence is at least bundledSequence, validUntil has not passed at nowSeconds (the whole day counts), and issuedAt is no more than one day after nowSeconds. A reject carries the reason its check must report. A missing signature is a reject. Every key is public.",
